IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-art02-making`

-- je21-art09-10-subordinate-powers: Articles 9 and 10 of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021):
-- 9 Powers to make Jersey subordinate legislation, 10 Power to incorporate technical documents by reference.
--
-- Article 9 gives every power to make Jersey subordinate legislation a set of incidents, "unless provision is made to the contrary" (an input wherever it appears).
-- The question the brief asks exactly: can an Order of a Minister (not made by the States, Article 2(3)(b)) use the incidental power of 9(5) to amend a Law (made by the States)?
-- The answer is 9(6)(b): no.
-- `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` below answers it from three inputs (who made the instrument, what is amended, whether provision is made to the contrary).
--
-- "made after 28th March 2003" (9(2)) is taken as the days after that day: legislation made on 28 March 2003 itself is not "after" it.
-- Forks registered here: L5 (what "made by the States" is, in je21-art02-making) and L6 (whether the limits of 9(6) bear on provision that is not an amendment).

§ `Article 9 -- Powers to make Jersey subordinate legislation`

§§ `9(1) The power may be exercised from time to time, and includes a power to repeal, amend or replace`

-- Answers: does Article 9(1) give a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation the incidents of being exercisable from time to time and including a power to repeal, amend or replace what was made,
-- the power to repeal, amend or replace being "exercisable in the same way and subject to the same conditions"?
-- It does for any power conferred by Jersey legislation "whenever made", unless provision is made to the contrary (an input).
-- src:91 | (1) Where any Jersey legislation (whenever made) confers a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation, unless provision is made to the contrary, the power may be exercised from time to time and includes a power to repeal, amend or replace the legislation made that is exercisable in the same way and subject to the same conditions.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(1) (src:91)
GIVEN `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 9(1): the power may be exercised from time to time and includes a power to repeal, amend or replace` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
        `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation`
    AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`

§§ `9(2) to 9(4) Variation by case, class, conditions, exceptions and factors; partial repeal`

-- Answers: does Article 9(2) let the power apply generally, or be limited, or make different provision for different cases or classes of case, or be limited by reference to stated conditions, exceptions or factors?
-- It does where the legislation conferring the power was made after 28 March 2003, unless provision is made to the contrary (an input).
-- For legislation made on or before 28 March 2003 the Article says nothing, and the model refuses.
-- src:92 | (2) Where any Jersey legislation made after 28th March 2003 confers a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation, the power may, unless provision is made to the contrary, be exercised –
-- src:93 | (a) to apply generally to all cases or be limited in its application to, or make different provision for different cases or classes of case; or
-- src:94 | (b) to apply generally or be limited in its application by reference to stated conditions, exceptions or factors.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(2) (src:92-94)
GIVEN `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` IS A DATE
      `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 9(2): the power may apply generally or be limited, or make different provision for different cases, classes, conditions, exceptions or factors` `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` AT MOST YMD 2003 3 28
    THEN REFUSE "Article 9(2) is confined to legislation made after 28th March 2003, and the Law does not say what holds for legislation made on or before that day"
    ELSE     `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation`
         AND NOT `provision is made to the contrary`

-- Answers: is provision about this number of cases within the power in Article 9(2)?
-- "a 'class' includes a single case", and the power "includes the power to make provision about any one or more cases", so one case is enough.
-- Provision about no case at all is not mentioned, and the model refuses.
-- src:95 | (3) The power in paragraph (2) includes the power to make provision about any one or more cases and for the purposes of that paragraph a “class” includes a single case.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(3) (src:95)
GIVEN `the number of cases the provision is about` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` IS A DATE
      `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 9(3): provision about that many cases is within the power in Article 9(2)` `the number of cases the provision is about` `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `the number of cases the provision is about` LESS THAN 1
    THEN REFUSE "Article 9(3) speaks of one or more cases and says nothing of provision about no case"
    ELSE `Article 9(2): the power may apply generally or be limited, or make different provision for different cases, classes, conditions, exceptions or factors` `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary`

-- Answers: may a provision that repeals legislation be brought into force only to the extent of repealing some of its provisions?
-- Article 9(4) says the power in 9(2) enables it, so the answer is the answer for 9(2).
-- src:96 | (4) The power in paragraph (2) enables a provision that repeals any legislation to be brought into force only to the extent of repealing some of its provisions.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(4) (src:96)
GIVEN `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` IS A DATE
      `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 9(4): a repeal may be brought into force in part` `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` MEANS
    `Article 9(2): the power may apply generally or be limited, or make different provision for different cases, classes, conditions, exceptions or factors` `the day on which the legislation conferring the power was made` `Jersey legislation confers the power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` `provision is made to the contrary`

§§ `9(5) and 9(6) Incidental, supplemental and consequential provision, and its limits`

-- Answers: does the incidental power of Article 9(5), limited by Article 9(6), authorise this provision?
--   `Article 9(5) authorises the provision`:                  the incidental power covers it.
--   `Article 9(6) bars the provision`:                        the limit in 9(6)(a) or (b) rules it out.
--   `Article 9(5) does not apply because provision is made to the contrary`: the Law cannot say what applies instead.
-- 9(6)(a), for Regulations (and Triennial Regulations): the power is limited to amending legislation other than the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000 or the legislation giving the power to make the Regulations.
-- 9(6)(b), for legislation not made by the States: the power is limited to amending other legislation not made by the States.
-- So an Order of a Minister, which is signed and not adopted (Article 2(3)(b)), can amend an Order and cannot amend a Law or Regulations.
-- Fork L5 gives "made by the States"; fork L6 says whether the limits bear on provision that is not an amendment.
-- 9(6) names Regulations and legislation not made by the States only.
-- An Act of the States is neither, so on the text neither limit bears on it; NOTES.md section 10 asks a domain expert whether that is intended.
-- src:97 | (5) Unless provision is made to the contrary, a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation also authorises the making of provision incidental to, supplemental to, or consequential upon that legislation.
-- src:98 | (6) However, the power in paragraph (5) is limited –
-- src:99 | (a) in the case of Regulations, to amending any legislation other than the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000 or the legislation giving the power to make the Regulations; and
-- src:100 | (b) in the case of any legislation not made by the States, to amending any other legislation not made by the States.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(5) and (6) (src:97-100)
GIVEN `the form of the instrument being made` IS A `Form of legislation`
      `the legislation to be amended` IS A `Legislation to be amended`
      `the provision is an amendment of other legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reading of legislation made by the States` IS A `Reading L5 of legislation made by the States`
      `the reading of the limits` IS A `Reading L6 of the limits in Article 9(6)`
GIVETH A `What the incidental power does`
`Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `the form of the instrument being made` `the legislation to be amended` `the provision is an amendment of other legislation` `provision is made to the contrary` `the reading of legislation made by the States` `the reading of the limits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `provision is made to the contrary`
            THEN `Article 9(5) does not apply because provision is made to the contrary`
        IF NOT `the provision is an amendment of other legislation`
            THEN CONSIDER `the reading of the limits`
                 WHEN `the limits bear on provision that amends other legislation, and incidental provision of any other kind is not limited by them`
                     THEN `Article 9(5) authorises the provision`
                 WHEN `the power in Article 9(5) is limited to amendments of the permitted kind, and authorises incidental provision of no other kind`
                     THEN `Article 9(6) bars the provision`
        OTHERWISE
            IF     `the limit in Article 9(6)(a) is met` `the form of the instrument being made` `the legislation to be amended`
               AND `the limit in Article 9(6)(b) is met` `the form of the instrument being made` `the legislation to be amended` `the reading of legislation made by the States`
            THEN `Article 9(5) authorises the provision`
            ELSE `Article 9(6) bars the provision`

-- 9(6)(a): met unless the instrument is Regulations and the legislation to be amended is the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000 or the legislation giving the power.
-- src:99 | (a) in the case of Regulations, to amending any legislation other than the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000 or the legislation giving the power to make the Regulations; and
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(6)(a) (src:99)
GIVEN `the form of the instrument being made` IS A `Form of legislation`
      `the legislation to be amended` IS A `Legislation to be amended`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the limit in Article 9(6)(a) is met` `the form of the instrument being made` `the legislation to be amended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the form of the instrument being made`
    WHEN `Regulations`
        THEN     NOT `the legislation to be amended`'s `it is the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000`
             AND NOT `the legislation to be amended`'s `it is the legislation giving the power to make the instrument`
    WHEN `Triennial Regulations`
        THEN     NOT `the legislation to be amended`'s `it is the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000`
             AND NOT `the legislation to be amended`'s `it is the legislation giving the power to make the instrument`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- 9(6)(b): met unless the instrument was not made by the States and the legislation to be amended was made by the States.
-- src:100 | (b) in the case of any legislation not made by the States, to amending any other legislation not made by the States.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(6)(b) (src:100)
GIVEN `the form of the instrument being made` IS A `Form of legislation`
      `the legislation to be amended` IS A `Legislation to be amended`
      `the reading of legislation made by the States` IS A `Reading L5 of legislation made by the States`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the limit in Article 9(6)(b) is met` `the form of the instrument being made` `the legislation to be amended` `the reading of legislation made by the States` MEANS
    IF `Article 2: the legislation was made by the States` `the form of the instrument being made` `the reading of legislation made by the States`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE NOT `Article 2: the legislation was made by the States` (`the legislation to be amended`'s `its form`) `the reading of legislation made by the States`

§§ `9(7) Made under all the powers under which it may be made`

-- Answers: is the subordinate legislation treated as made in exercise of this power?
-- It is if it is stated to be made under a power conferred by legislation (including this Law) and it may be made under this power.
-- src:101 | (7) Where Jersey subordinate legislation is stated to be made under any power conferred by any legislation (including this Law) it is treated as being made in exercise of all the powers under which it may be made.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 9(7) (src:101)
GIVEN `it is stated to be made under a power conferred by legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it may be made under this power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 9(7): the subordinate legislation is treated as made in exercise of this power` `it is stated to be made under a power conferred by legislation` `it may be made under this power` MEANS
        `it is stated to be made under a power conferred by legislation`
    AND `it may be made under this power`

§ `Article 10 -- Power to incorporate technical documents by reference`

-- Answers: does Article 10 reach this document?
-- Article 10(1) lets the States amend a Law so that its power to make subordinate legislation includes incorporating by reference a technical document, other than legislation from any jurisdiction, that is accessible to the public without charge.
-- 10(2): a technical document is one concerned with the practices, procedures, processes or requirements for use of a technical product and aimed at a person with particular knowledge or experience in that technical field.
-- Article 10 gives the States the power to amend; it does not amend any Law itself.
-- So unless the Law that gives the power has been amended by Regulations under Article 10(1) (an input), the model refuses.
-- If it has, the answer is whether the document is of the kind Article 10 reaches; whether it is incorporated as it is at a particular time or from time to time is what that amendment says.
-- src:103 | (1) The States may by Regulations amend any Law to provide that the power to make subordinate legislation under that Law includes the power to incorporate by reference any technical document (other than legislation from any jurisdiction) that is accessible to the public without charge as it is in force –
-- src:104 | (a) at a particular time; or
-- src:105 | (b) from time to time.
-- src:106 | (2) In paragraph (1) “technical document” means a document that is concerned with the practices, procedures, processes or requirements for use of a technical product and which is aimed at a person with particular knowledge or experience in that technical field.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 10(1) and (2) (src:103-106)
GIVEN `the Law giving the power has been amended by Regulations under Article 10(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `Facts about a document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 10: the power to make subordinate legislation includes incorporating the document by reference` `the Law giving the power has been amended by Regulations under Article 10(1)` document MEANS
    IF NOT `the Law giving the power has been amended by Regulations under Article 10(1)`
    THEN REFUSE "Article 10 gives the States power to amend a Law to allow incorporation by reference and does not itself allow it, and no such amendment is given"
    ELSE     NOT document's `it is legislation from some jurisdiction`
         AND document's `it is accessible to the public without charge`
         AND document's `it is concerned with the practices, procedures, processes or requirements for use of a technical product`
         AND document's `it is aimed at a person with particular knowledge or experience in that technical field`
